scope: |
  Sergiy asked for `Cons.join` after rozum hit its absence. Delivered as a std EXTENSION, not a core
  List method: `join` is JS vocabulary, not Scala's (Scala says mkString), and this project's List is
  meant to be the real Scala one. An extension in .ssc is portable across every lane by construction
  -- probed on native and --v1, identical output, zero runtime edits -- whereas a core method has to
  be added twice and is exactly how the two lanes drift apart.
next: write the module + a conformance case that runs on BOTH lanes
